==============================================================================
    driftwood moves its nist pin to 2.0.0. platform stays on 1.0.0.
    REFUSED: diamond: nist (controls) is inherited at 2 versions -> 1.0.0 via driftwood -> platform -> nist , driftwood -> platform -> nist; 2.0.0 via driftwood -> nist
    REFUSED: 3 control(s) in the baseline have no live implementation
    REFUSED: 1 workload(s) pin a version the composed array no longer declares
      uncovered nist-800-53:ac-6: no policy claims this control at all
      uncovered nist-800-53:cm-6: no policy claims this control at all
      uncovered nist-800-53:ac-6.10: no policy claims this control at all
      orphan driftwood-app pins 1.0.0

    Two refusals at once, and they are different failures. The diamond
    splits, AND the new control ac-6.10 has no implementation anywhere.
    At nist this bump only ADDS a control. Nothing existing changed.
    At driftwood it breaks the build. The bump is institution-relative,
    which is ticket cs-02's finding seen from the other side.

